; The one variable: an `owner_uid_path` that ends inside instance content. `owner="Gone"` names
; no node, so Godot follows the trail (948136725, 1273451906) to `Player/Inner` and takes the
; owner table of that node (packed_scene.cpp:1947-2005). `Lamp` claims `%Lamp` there, so Shade
; sits under Lamp, left of the origin and up. Without the trail the table is empty and Shade
; re-roots to the file root. No other golden carries an `owner_uid_path`.

